# Underfoot Underdogs {2}{R}, 1/2: entering makes a 1/1 red Goblin token. On turn 3 {1},{T}: the Goblin (power 1) is aimed at and
# can't be blocked this turn, so Bot2's Ornithopter may not block it (it is refused) and Bot2 takes 1. Hill Giant (power 3) is
# too strong to be the target and Bot2's Ornithopter is not Bot1's: both refused. The Underdogs is summoning sick on turn 1 and
# can't pay {T} then, though the mana was there.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Underfoot Underdogs
Hill Giant
Mountain x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Underfoot Underdogs.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire; Mox Emerald; Underfoot Underdogs; Goblin Token
! Bot1.Battlefield.Underfoot Underdogs.Activate(Ability: can't be blocked; Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hill Giant.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
! Bot1.Battlefield.Underfoot Underdogs.Activate(Ability: can't be blocked; Bot1.Battlefield.Hill Giant)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Underfoot Underdogs.Activate(Ability: can't be blocked; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Underfoot Underdogs.Activate(Ability: can't be blocked; Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Goblin Token > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Goblin Token)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Underfoot Underdogs.Tapped = true
